			<div class="content" id="post-content-2198991">
									

<p>I don't think I like these because most of them have physical effects that are related in some way to the function of the object, like being able to do what the object normally does but super well, while the original object had two effects both mental rather than physical, the first of which was just an odd effect that made it less useful and the second is something very subtle that you wouldn't expect the object to do. The effects just don't have the same feel as the original. I would like it if some of the objects had more subtle effects or had mental effects like original. I also don't like that too many of them have useful or cool effects.</p>
<p>Edit:<br />
it also would have been interesting if you had written them such that the effects of the objects seemed like they were meant to be used together, having effects that go together or complement each other somehow. It also would have been more interesting if you had written the effects in a way that seemed to tell a subtle story about why the objects have their effects.</p>

