			<div class="content" id="post-content-2199903">
									

<p>See, the similarities between this and <em>The Lost Room</em> bug me. Specifically, both the comb in <em>The Lost Room</em> and this mess with/slow down time. I'm not accusing anyone of plagiarism, mostly because I credit TroyL as being way smarter and creative than that and because I don't feel I need to be opening cans of worms like that right now, but the similarity is too great for me to ignore. More than that, while I do find it plausible that the Foundation might rediscover and declassify (within its own ranks, anyway) this information, and that the same agent who figured out what the CI was up to would rediscover this info (or write the preface to it, at least), I wasn't very entertained. These are overpowered anomalous items that happened to come in the same package. This doesn't make a compelling narrative like the original SCP. Neutral vote for now.</p>

